# Settings for `docker compose up -d`. Copy to .env and uncomment what you want to change.
# Without a .env file the hub listens on http://localhost:6230, on this machine only, with data in a Docker volume.

# Address and port on this machine. 0.0.0.0 lets other machines connect: use HTTPS in front for anything
# beyond a trusted network (docs/deploy.md).
# HUB_BIND=0.0.0.0
# HUB_PORT=6230

# The address people type into their browser; used in the links the hub prints.
# HUB_PUBLIC_URL=http://hub.example.org:6230

# Where the data lives. A folder on this machine instead of the default Docker volume; create it first so it
# belongs to you. The hub runs as the folder's owner.
# HUB_DATA=/srv/research_hub

# Set to 1 when a reverse proxy terminates HTTPS in front of the hub.
# HUB_TRUST_PROXY=1

# First start only: create the admin account, and optionally a first project, without opening the setup link.
# Ignored once an admin exists. The password needs at least 10 characters; change it after signing in, and
# remove these lines afterwards.
# HUB_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.org
# HUB_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# HUB_ADMIN_NAME=you
# HUB_FIRST_PROJECT=my-project
